  "gloss": "humidification; adding moisture",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "humidification; adding moisture to the air",
      "explanation": "Raising the moisture level of the air, typically to counter dryness in winter or in heated, air-conditioned rooms. Takes する to become a verb."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29748_kashitsu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{部屋|へや}を{加湿|かしつ}する。",
      "english": "Humidify the room.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29748_kashitsu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{冬|ふゆ}は{加湿|かしつ}が{大切|たいせつ}だ。",
      "english": "Humidification is important in winter.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29748_kashitsu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{乾燥|かんそう}する{季節|きせつ}には、{加湿器|かしつき}で{部屋|へや}を{加湿|かしつ}するとよい。",
      "english": "In the dry season, it is good to humidify the room with a humidifier.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{加|くわ}える (to add) + {湿|しめ}り (moisture). Raising the humidity of a space, usually for comfort and health in dry conditions.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {加湿器|かしつき}: humidifier\n- {加湿|かしつ}{機能|きのう}: humidifying function\n- {部屋|へや}を{加湿|かしつ}する: to humidify a room\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {除湿|じょしつ}: dehumidification — the opposite; removing moisture from the air",
